# {{ title }}

Auto-generated IsaacLab IL extension for the **{{ task_id }}** task.

## Installation

```bash
cd {{ project_dir_name }}
pip install -e source/{{ package_name }}
```

The editable install writes `{{ package_name }}_register.pth` into your
site-packages, which auto-imports `{{ package_name }}` on Python startup. That
import side-effects `gym.register(...)` for `{{ task_id }}`{% if mimic is not none %} and `{{ mimic.mimic_task_id }}`{% endif %},
so IsaacLab's stock launch scripts can find your task without any per-task
patching.

## Usage

Run IsaacLab's scripts directly — no per-project copies are needed:

```bash
# Teleop the task
./isaaclab.sh -p scripts/environments/teleoperation/teleop_se3_agent.py --task {{ task_id }}

{% if mimic is not none %}
# Record annotated demos for the Mimic data-generation pipeline
./isaaclab.sh -p scripts/tools/record_annotated_demos.py --task {{ mimic.mimic_task_id }}

{% endif %}
# Or run with random / zero actions
./isaaclab.sh -p scripts/environments/random_agent.py --task {{ task_id }}
./isaaclab.sh -p scripts/environments/zero_agent.py --task {{ task_id }}
```

Useful teleop flags:

- `--teleop_device handtracking` (pink_ik tasks) or `keyboard` / `spacemouse` / `gamepad`
- `--dataset_dir ./datasets/{{ task_name }} --dataset_file run0` to override the recorder's HDF5 target
- `--enable_pinocchio` when the task uses pink_ik

## Project Structure

```
source/{{ package_name }}/{{ package_name }}/
├── assets/          # USD scene, object, and robot files
├── base_il_env/     # Base IL environment (shared across tasks)
└── tasks/           # Task-specific configurations and MDP functions
```

## Customization

- Edit `tasks/manager_based/{{ task_name }}/{{ task_name }}_cfg.py` for task configuration
- Add custom MDP functions in `tasks/manager_based/{{ task_name }}/mdp/`
- Place USD files in the `assets/` subdirectories
